<section>
  ## Code options: alignment

  Alignment: `halign=` and `valign=` (`start` | `center` | `end`), or the classes `left` `center` `right` and `top` `middle` `bottom` in `class=`.
  Without them the code follows its slide: `start`, unless the slide says otherwise.
  Other options: `id` (the animation), classes `lines` and `panel`, `title=`, `size=`, `fit=none`, `focus=`, `transition=` (see the next slides).

  <code lang=typescript id=g1 class=left>
    <frame>
      const where = "left";
    </frame>
    <frame>
      const where = "still left, now longer";
    </frame>
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  ## Code options: size

  `size=14` fixes the font size in pixels. Without it the code is scaled to fit,
  using the largest frame of the section, so the size never jumps between frames.

  <code lang=typescript id=g2 size=14>
    <frame>
      const small = "size=14";
    </frame>
    <frame>
      const small = "size=14, and the same font size in every frame";
    </frame>
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  ## Code options: `class="right top"`

  <code lang=typescript class="right top">
    const corner = "top right";
  </code>
</section>

<notes>
  Options are attributes of the tag: <code lang=ts class=left size=18>
</notes>

<notes>
  Next: focus=, fit and size in detail.
</notes>
